      "math_academy_id": "q-72739",
      "sequence_position": 14,
      "problem": "Suppose $B$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(B)=11.$ What is the value of $det(2B)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2B) & ={2}^{5}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =32\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =352.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
